  "overview": {
    "en": "Steven Weinberg was an American theoretical physicist who unified the electromagnetic and weak nuclear forces into the electroweak interaction. He shared the 1979 Nobel Prize in Physics and was considered one of the most influential physicists of the late 20th century.",
